-- Tool face: the game's own mode strip, moved into the capsule. The game
-- button keeps the state and the handler; this face only mirrors it. Built
-- outside New for the same register-ceiling reason as the idle face.
--
-- Sizes match the game's own strip (96 x 18 label over a 96 x 24 button, both
-- 14 px) so the tap target never moves. The skin is the hub's: dark glass,
-- hairline rim, mode colour on the icon and the text only.
local TOOL_ICON = "lucide:hammer"

-- Creator.Icon returns one table, not two values: [1] is the image, [2] the
-- rect record. Reading it as a tuple left the rect at 0, 0 and the glyph blank.
local function PaintToolIcon(Image, Name)
	local Data = Creator.Icon(Name or TOOL_ICON)
	local Rect = Data[2]
	Image.Image = Data[1]
	Image.ImageRectOffset = Rect.ImageRectPosition
	Image.ImageRectSize = Rect.ImageRectSize
end

